hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
1651.1,
1651.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam that Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari said
1652.1,Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard that Umar ibn al- Khattab said
1652.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that he heard that Umar ibn al- Khattab said
1653.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamim that Ibn Sirin said
1653.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Ayyub ibn Abi Tamim that Ibn Sirin said
1654.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar wore garments dyed with red earth and dyed with saffron
1654.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar wore garments dyed with red earth and dyed with saffron
1655.1,"It was narrated to me from Malik, from Ibn Shihab, that he was asked about the prescribed punishment for a slave concerning wine. He said: It has reached me that he receives half the prescribed punishment of a free person concerning wine. And that Umar ibn al-Khattab, Uthman ibn Affan, and Abdullah ibn Umar had flogged their slaves half the prescribed punishment of a free person concerning wine."
1655.2,"It was narrated to me from Malik, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, will not look on the Day of Resurrection at him who drags his garment out of arrogance."
1656.1,Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha the wife of the Prophet
1656.2,Malik related to me from Hisham ibn Urwa from his father that A'isha the wife of the Prophet
1657.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Alqama ibn Abi Alqama that his mother said
1657.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Alqama ibn Abi Alqama that his mother said
1658.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam from Abu Salih that Abu Hurayra said
1658.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Muslim ibn Abi Maryam from Abu Salih that Abu Hurayra said
1659.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Ibn Shihab that the Messenger of Allah
1659.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Yahya ibn Said from Ibn Shihab that the Messenger of Allah
1660.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah
1660.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abdullah ibn Dinar from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah
1661.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah
1661.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah
1662.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi and Abdullah ibn Dinar and Zayd ibn Aslam that all of them informed him from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah
1662.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi and Abdullah ibn Dinar and Zayd ibn Aslam that all of them informed him from Abdullah ibn Umar that the Messenger of Allah
1663.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from al Ala ibn Abd ar-Rahman that his father said
1663.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from al Ala ibn Abd ar-Rahman that his father said
1664.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Bakr ibn Nafi from his father Nafi
1664.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu Bakr ibn Nafi from his father Nafi
1665.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah
1665.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah
1666.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah
1666.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj from Abu Hurayra that the Messenger of Allah
1667.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from his paternal uncle Abu Suhayl ibn Malik from his father that Kab al-Ahbar said to a man who took off his sandals
1667.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from his paternal uncle Abu Suhayl ibn Malik from his father that Kab al-Ahbar said to a man who took off his sandals
1668.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj that Abu Hurayra said
1668.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Abu'z-Zinad from al-Araj that Abu Hurayra said
1669.1,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab saw a silk robe at the door of the mosque. He said
1669.2,Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi from Abdullah ibn Umar that Umar ibn al-Khattab saw a silk robe at the door of the mosque. He said
1670.1,"Yahya related to me from Malik from Da'ud ibn al-Husayn that
Waqid ibn Amr ibn Sad ibn Muadh informed him from Mahmud ibn Labid al-
Ansari that when Umar ibn al-Khattab went to ash-Sham, the people of
ash-Sham complained to him about the bad air of their land and its
heaviness. They said, ""Only this drink helps."" Umar said, ""Drink this
honey preparation."" They said, ""Honey does not help us."" A man from
the people of that land said, ""Can we give you something of this drink
which does not intoxicate?"" He said, ""Yes."" They cooked it until two-
thirds of it evaporated and one-third of it remained. Then they
brought it to Umar. Umar put his finger in it and then lifted his head
and extended it. He said, ""This is fruit juice concentrated by
boiling. This is like the distillation with which you smear the
camel's scabs."" Umar ordered them to drink it. Ubada ibn as-Samit said
to him, ""You have made it halal, by Allah!"" Umar said, ""No, by Allah!
O Allah! I will not make anything halal for them which You have made
haram for them! I will not make anything haram for them which You have
made halal for them."""
1670.2,Yahya related to me from Malik that Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha said
